  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nHeading into the end of the week and through the weekend, the\nupper level ridging pattern will continue building over the\nregion, keeping mid-level heights raised, with 850mb\ntemperatures between 13-16C. With a continued minimal difference\n(2-3 degrees) between the 25th and 75th percentiles, there's\nhigh confidence in afternoon highs remaining in the upper 70s to\neven the low 80s through Monday.\n\nThe aforementioned upper level low currently over the west \ncoast looks to pivot northeast into the Northern Plains by \nTuesday of next week. Models however are still in disagreement \nregarding the exact track, which would influence our rain \nchances. Right now, chances of rainfall midweek continues to \ndecrease, with the likely scenario keeping our area dry through \nat least Wednesday afternoon. It's still fairly far out, so \nseveral variable still need to come into better agreement before\nour confidence increases in the precipitation forecast.",
